{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "02NO", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\Rightarrow$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathbf{P}^n_S$", "MATH_0003": "$S$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-ample-over-affine}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-quasi-projective-finite-type-over-S}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{constructions-lemma-projective-space-bundle}", "REF_0004": "\\ref{lemma-ample-very-ample}", "REF_0005": "\\ref{lemma-ample-power-ample}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:4c39aa9608dd459ff8c87e8730f5a6647e34f471b20763f6af164c744e90e768", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:a4d929f93764f3c7f3a1664ce4575bc925b28b5ef6dbbbfc5871d94f3d48ba9e", "source_text": "The equivalence of (1) and (2) is Lemma <REF_0001>.\nThe implication (2) <MATH_0001> (6) is\nLemma <REF_0002>.\nTrivially (6) implies (5).\nAs <MATH_0002> is a projective bundle over <MATH_0003> (see\nConstructions, Lemma <REF_0003>)\nwe see that\n(5) implies (3) and (6) implies (4) from the definition of a\nrelatively very ample sheaf.\nTrivially (4) implies (3). To finish we have to show that\n(3) implies (2) which follows from Lemma <REF_0004>\nand Lemma <REF_0005>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:ecc2f05ede3e146ac05d09b0049e1786bc896e12def7223d6c831a1b3e4dc93f", "unit_id": "tag:01VT:proof"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "02NO", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f : X \\to S$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{L}$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{O}_X$", "MATH_0004": "$S$", "MATH_0005": "$f$", "MATH_0006": "$\\mathcal{L}$", "MATH_0007": "$f$", "MATH_0008": "$\\mathcal{L}^{\\otimes d}$", "MATH_0009": "$f$", "MATH_0010": "$d \\geq 1$", "MATH_0011": "$\\mathcal{L}^{\\otimes d}$", "MATH_0012": "$f$", "MATH_0013": "$d \\gg 1$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\item", "STRUCT_0005": "\\end{enumerate}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-finite-type-ample-very-ample}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:0e4babea059a535cacc9b508a766bebd9a1a1d513c2e4c4dd3f1dfa31230da2b", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:635c13f84cccb3644ae32ae314b925170d510c75f5c6e9419d657d436f30aa41", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a morphism of schemes.\nLet <MATH_0002> be an invertible <MATH_0003>-module.\nAssume <MATH_0004> quasi-compact and <MATH_0005> of finite type.\nThe following are equivalent\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> <MATH_0006> is <MATH_0007>-ample,\n<STRUCT_0003> <MATH_0008> is <MATH_0009>-very ample for some <MATH_0010>,\n<STRUCT_0004> <MATH_0011> is <MATH_0012>-very ample for all <MATH_0013>.\n<STRUCT_0005>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:c937d4eab1dc5caebb995c1205c1f8077e3d782bb0a412a87687a3723b61794d", "unit_id": "tag:01VU:statement"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "02NO", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{L}$", "MATH_0002": "$f$", "MATH_0003": "$S = V_1 \\cup \\ldots \\cup V_m$", "MATH_0004": "$X_i = f^{-1}(V_i)$", "MATH_0005": "$d_0$", "MATH_0006": "$\\mathcal{L}^{\\otimes d}$", "MATH_0007": "$X_i/V_i$", "MATH_0008": "$d \\geq d_0$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-ample-very-ample}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-finite-type-over-affine-ample-very-ample}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{lemma-relatively-very-ample}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:906266da60b02858b5c01bb9332819d5a70058f4bab4bd6a20f3b27f947e7578", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:92a7922da0f66e793a16156ff530aee0b1fabd67c9b53d57da23b5a87ae80dd8", "source_text": "Trivially (3) implies (2). Lemma <REF_0001> guarantees that\n(2) implies (1) since a morphism of finite type is quasi-compact\nby definition. Assume that <MATH_0001> is <MATH_0002>-ample. Choose a finite affine\nopen covering <MATH_0003>. Write <MATH_0004>.\nBy Lemma <REF_0002> above we see\nthere exists a <MATH_0005> such that <MATH_0006> is\nrelatively very ample on <MATH_0007> for all <MATH_0008>. Hence we conclude\n(1) implies (3) by Lemma <REF_0003>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:7d60531ad49e38387a87f2381b069206c8a9f7a93fc92b7fd57cc004d9f5720e", "unit_id": "tag:01VU:proof"}
